that based on the photo evidence I have,

02:40:42.150 --> 02:40:45.530
you may have some of that, that I shared with Anna.

02:40:46.430 --> 02:40:47.550
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

02:40:47.650 --> 02:40:47.990
We, yeah.

02:40:48.070 --> 02:40:49.790
In fact, it's going to come out on our pod

02:40:49.790 --> 02:40:51.990
where she shows some really interesting photos.

02:40:52.110 --> 02:40:53.970
Well, you see photos with people in them

02:40:53.970 --> 02:40:56.470
or children or animals.

02:40:57.200 --> 02:40:58.360
Where did I get that?

02:40:58.740 --> 02:40:59.780
How did I get those?

02:40:59.780 --> 02:41:00.160
And,

02:41:00.160 --> 02:41:02.860
this was right after the lady came.

02:41:03.500 --> 02:41:06.320
And at that time, I didn't have a video camera.

02:41:06.740 --> 02:41:09.340
I had a cell phone, the flip phone, right?

02:41:10.740 --> 02:41:12.880
But I went out and bought a little pocket camera,

02:41:12.980 --> 02:41:13.840
a little Instamatic.

02:41:14.620 --> 02:41:17.960
And I started taking just every night.

02:41:18.460 --> 02:41:20.460
I wasn't able to get anything before,

02:41:20.580 --> 02:41:22.760
but from that point forward, I did.

02:41:22.880 --> 02:41:24.440
And it's like my dog died.

02:41:24.500 --> 02:41:25.880
I write about this in the book.

02:41:26.440 --> 02:41:29.560
I was with Tim at Cape Canaveral for a week.

02:41:30.510 --> 02:41:33.810
And some guys from the NRO and we were meeting

02:41:33.810 --> 02:41:36.910
and at a launch and had been there all week.

02:41:36.970 --> 02:41:37.790
And it was Saturday.

02:41:38.270 --> 02:41:40.030
Launch finally went off Saturday.

02:41:41.230 --> 02:41:42.150
Delayed all week.

02:41:44.060 --> 02:41:46.460
My wife knew I was coming home at Sunday morning

02:41:46.460 --> 02:41:47.800
or Sunday night.

02:41:47.940 --> 02:41:50.120
I was going to leave after the launch, Saturday night,

02:41:50.240 --> 02:41:51.460
get up Sunday morning, drive home.

02:41:52.380 --> 02:41:55.090
So at four o'clock, it was over.

02:41:55.290 --> 02:41:57.070
I said, Tim, I'm going to Fayetteville.

02:41:57.330 --> 02:41:59.210
So I got my car and I took off.

02:42:00.500 --> 02:42:01.400
Didn't tell anybody.

02:42:01.620 --> 02:42:02.640
Drove all night long.

02:42:02.780 --> 02:42:03.240
All night.

02:42:04.200 --> 02:42:07.800
Pulled over to rest areas, 13 hours, right from my house there.

02:42:07.960 --> 02:42:09.360
Pulled over and took a nap.

02:42:10.180 --> 02:42:12.940
8.30 Sunday morning, I drove in the yard.

02:42:13.880 --> 02:42:16.960
When I drove in the yard, I knew immediately

02:42:16.960 --> 02:42:20.030
that my Labrador was dead.

02:42:22.220 --> 02:42:23.000
I knew it.

02:42:23.100 --> 02:42:23.840
I knew it.

02:42:24.200 --> 02:42:26.100
I can't tell you how I knew it, but I knew it.

02:42:26.460 --> 02:42:28.060
Just came right into my mind.

02:42:28.120 --> 02:42:28.880
I saw it all.

02:42:28.880 --> 02:42:29.580
I felt it.

02:42:31.040 --> 02:42:33.940
My kids and family had buried her in the backyard.

02:42:33.940 --> 02:42:36.800
And three days before, never told me

02:42:36.800 --> 02:42:38.320
because they didn't want me upset, right?

02:42:38.360 --> 02:42:41.860
It was like my child, this 90-pound Labrador,

02:42:42.040 --> 02:42:43.400
female named Nellie.

02:42:45.380 --> 02:42:47.140
I opened the front door and walked in.

02:42:47.220 --> 02:42:51.060
My wife's asleep at the front door in the living room on the couch.

02:42:51.540 --> 02:42:52.480
House full of kids.

02:42:52.600 --> 02:42:53.820
They'd been up all weekend.

02:42:53.940 --> 02:42:55.300
They had invited all their friends.

02:42:55.420 --> 02:42:57.480
So mom kind of would stay near the front

02:42:57.480 --> 02:42:58.800
where all the bedrooms were.

02:42:58.920 --> 02:43:01.480
Our little girl, she was the only girl, right?

02:43:01.540 --> 02:43:04.440
So mom's doing, she's doing her patrol.

02:43:04.840 --> 02:43:06.920
To keep any boys away from her.

02:43:07.020 --> 02:43:08.380
That's what moms do.

02:43:08.460 --> 02:43:11.300
So I walk in the door and I open it.

02:43:11.340 --> 02:43:12.300
She looks up at me.

02:43:12.340 --> 02:43:13.760
I said, what happened to my dog?

02:43:14.920 --> 02:43:15.880
And her eyes got big.

02:43:16.060 --> 02:43:18.040
And she said, oh my God, how did you know?

02:43:18.240 --> 02:43:19.540
I said, well, I felt her.

02:43:20.960 --> 02:43:22.540
She said, well, she ran out in the road

02:43:22.540 --> 02:43:23.900
and got run over by a car.

02:43:24.420 --> 02:43:26.500
And we buried her in the backyard.

02:43:27.680 --> 02:43:30.540
So I took and I thought about it all day.

02:43:31.440 --> 02:43:33.900
And that night I thought, she don't know she's dead.

02:43:34.340 --> 02:43:35.360
That's how I knew it.

02:43:35.420 --> 02:43:36.420
Because when I turned off,

02:43:36.500 --> 02:43:37.880
the road right where she was killed,

02:43:38.000 --> 02:43:40.800
it just kind of felt her and saw her in my thoughts.

02:43:41.850 --> 02:43:43.510
So I took a little white candle.

02:43:43.670 --> 02:43:46.110
I went out to her grave and I lit it.

02:43:46.390 --> 02:43:49.230
And I told her, I said, I'll be with you again.

02:43:49.750 --> 02:43:50.890
Just go to the light.

02:43:51.550 --> 02:43:53.310
And she comes up out of her grave

02:43:53.310 --> 02:43:54.410
and a little ball of light.

02:43:54.470 --> 02:43:55.490
And I took that picture.

02:43:56.780 --> 02:43:57.880
And that's how I got there.

02:43:58.320 --> 02:43:58.680
Wow.

02:43:59.990 --> 02:44:00.790
That's amazing.

02:44:00.790 --> 02:44:02.610
And you should have a copy of it.

02:44:02.690 --> 02:44:04.230
I would love to see that.

02:44:04.430 --> 02:44:04.670
Yeah.

02:44:05.110 --> 02:44:06.590
We could put that up.

02:44:06.790 --> 02:44:07.350
So what is that?

02:44:07.350 --> 02:44:08.010
What does that tell you?

02:44:08.390 --> 02:44:10.170
You know, what does that tell you?

02:44:10.210 --> 02:44:12.370
And I've got people, lots of people and children.

02:44:12.570 --> 02:44:13.650
In fact, I have a child.

02:44:13.730 --> 02:44:15.170
My wife and I lost a child.

02:44:15.530 --> 02:44:18.730
We have four, but we lost a child.

02:44:19.010 --> 02:44:22.620
And I was out thinking about him.

02:44:23.380 --> 02:44:28.220
And this lonely orb, there it comes.

02:44:31.080 --> 02:44:32.380
And I took a picture of it.

02:44:32.380 --> 02:44:34.260
And there was a child.

02:44:36.140 --> 02:44:36.420
Yeah.

02:44:36.680 --> 02:44:37.540
In the orb.

02:44:37.680 --> 02:44:38.240
In the orb.

02:44:38.320 --> 02:44:39.960
And this is my screenshot.

02:44:40.900 --> 02:44:41.460
Wow.

02:44:41.460 --> 02:44:42.300
I'll show you.

02:44:44.900 --> 02:44:46.260
Oh, my God.

02:44:46.560 --> 02:44:47.660
That's a real photo.

02:44:47.760 --> 02:44:51.320
That's a photo of a child in a ball of light.

02:44:51.880 --> 02:44:53.300
That's a real photo.

02:44:53.560 --> 02:44:53.880
Yeah.

02:44:54.360 --> 02:44:55.740
